<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fyodor Funtikov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1926">1926</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fyodor Funtikov was a Russian railway worker and Socialist Revolutionary who headed the Transcaspian Provisional Government formed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashgabat">Ashgabat</a> in July 1918 against Soviet rule. His government sought British help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. He was later accused of involvement in the execution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/26-baku-commissars">26 Baku Commissars</a> and was tried and shot by the Soviet authorities in 1926.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fyodor-funtikov.jpg" alt="Fyodor Funtikov" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Рамзин, К., ред. · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fyodor_Funtikov.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
